    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d194">

                <pb facs="0194" n="182" xml:id="pg182"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/12944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-07-09T00:00:00+02:00">July 9,
                            1941—midnight</date>.<lb/>[Received July 9—8:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2920. For the President and Acting Secretary.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d194-f1"/> My
                    2911, July 9, 8 p.m.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d194-f2"/> Mr. Eden has informed me
                    the Cabinet agreed this evening to conclusion of agreement with Russia in form
                    of joint declaration. Sir Stafford Cripps has been so advised but formal
                    proposal to Stalin cannot be made until after consultation with Dominions’
                    Governments which is being done by cable.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
